__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Scraper output that is written every run but read by nothing, and so was
# pure repo weight. Measured over the full history (2434 commits, Jul-Sep):
# activity.json cost 69.5MB of blob storage and latest.json 11.3MB, because
# both are rewritten wholesale each run and git re-stores a near-full blob
# every time. The scrapers still WRITE them, so they remain available locally
# for debugging and still get published to Pages by the "Assemble site" step —
# they just stop being committed.
#
#   activity.json — full-event trade feed. Superseded by trades_window.jsonl
#                   (rolling 6h, every trade) and alerts.jsonl (>$100). Its
#                   only reader, notify_large_trades.py, is not wired into any
#                   workflow.
#   latest.json   — raw Kalshi API dump, "for reference/debugging". Nothing
#                   reads it; snapshot.json is the normalized form everything
#                   actually uses.
data/activity.json
data/*/activity.json
data/*/*/latest.json
.claude/settings.local.json
.large_trade_seen.txt
